{
  "about": "color-mix() as CSS Color 5 section 3 defines it, each row as set on fillStyle: `expected` is what this library reads back, `null` where it refuses the string; `chrome`, `chromePixel` and `chromeStop` are what Chrome reads back, paints on an 8-bit canvas and whether its addColorStop takes it. Read by src/node/utils.rs and tests/suite/color-mix.test.js. A row without `why` agrees with Chrome to its six figures and its pixel to one level.",
  "source": "Chrome 156.0.8078.49 headless, a 1x1 canvas outside a document, measured 2026-10-28.",
  "why": {
    "draft": "CSS Color 5's grammar takes one or more colours, `[ <color> && <percentage [0,100]>? ]#`; Chrome 156 takes exactly two. docs/browser-differences.md.",
    "reference": "Chrome's figures stray from CSS Color 4's sample code worked in f64 from the fifth figure; this library's are that arithmetic at f32 precision. docs/browser-differences.md.",
    "rec2020": "rec2020 decodes by CSS Color 4's 2.4 gamma here and by BT.2020's curve in Chrome 156. docs/browser-differences.md.",
    "junk": "Chrome 156's addColorStop takes a colour followed by other text, which its fillStyle refuses; this library refuses both."
  },
